text:
I totally disagree (with the Satish Bhat editorial in IJMS); I read the Lancet editorial and I think it is on point; I did not see any political agenda or bias;  western press was equally critical of the Trump fiasco of managing the covid crisis here in the US in 2020;
We as health providers and researchers AND indians that are "sensitive" about bad and unfair messaging about our homeland, need to get over it and advocate for what's in the best interest of the average indian in india; and NOT distract against real or perceived villains; the issue is NOT "vulture journalism", or what the western journalists intentions are, etc;  
the issue is for the world to rally and help support india's current covid catastrophe (e.g provide supplies and get rid of the IP limits, as the Biden administration is belatedly doing); AND for india (and indians) to do the right thing:  universal vaccination messaging by using all available leadership in the country;  this can't be gov't sponsored bashing of western press, to make any gov't look good or bad;  facts are facts;  we have an unfolding tragedy, even if it means it makes you and your country  "look bad";

